message.content:
Make these changes across 3 files:

FILE 1: ui/web/js/sidebar.js
Find where the CSS stylesheet link is injected (the <link> element creation around line 16-19). BEFORE that link element, add a second <link> element that loads Google Fonts:

const fontLink = document.createElement("link");
fontLink.rel = "stylesheet";
fontLink.href = "https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap";
document.head.appendChild(fontLink);

Then find the send button click handler and the input keydown Enter handler. IMMEDIATELY when the user hits send (before the WebSocket message is sent), do two things:
a) Add the user's message bubble to the chat area right away (don't wait for server)
b) Show a "thinking" state: create a small element with class "sd-thinking" that says "Connecting to agents..." with a pulsing jade dot, and append it to the messages area

Clear the sd-thinking element when the first event (agent_dispatch, text_delta, or stage) arrives from the WebSocket.

FILE 2: ui/web/css/superduper.css
Find the --sd-font-sans and --sd-font-mono variable declarations. Change them to:
  --sd-font-sans: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --sd-font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;

Then add at the end of the file:

/* Thinking indicator — shown immediately on send */
.sd-thinking {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-sm);
  padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
  color: #888;
  font-family: var(--sd-font-sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.65;
  animation: sdSlideUp 0.3s var(--ease-out-expo);
}

@keyframes sdSlideUp {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); }
  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
}

.sd-thinking__dot {
  width: 8px;
  height: 8px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--agent-router);
  animation: sd-think-pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes sd-think-pulse {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
  50% { opacity: 0.4; transform: scale(0.85); }
}

FILE 3: ui/web/js/sidebar.js (continued)
Find the WebSocket message handlers. When "agent_dispatch" OR "text_delta" OR "stage" event arrives, check if the sd-thinking element exists and remove it:

const thinkingEl = messagesEl.querySelector(".sd-thinking");
if (thinkingEl) thinkingEl.remove();

This gives instant feedback on send — no more dead air.

