Make these changes to connect the chat and canvas visually:

FILE 1: ui/web/js/sidebar.js

Find where agent_status events are handled. When an agent_status event includes a "nodes_touched" array (which _extract_nodes_touched in routes.py already produces), dispatch a custom DOM event so node_fx.js can pick it up:

if (data.nodes_touched && data.nodes_touched.length > 0) {
  for (const nodeId of data.nodes_touched) {
    document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("superduper:node_touch", {
      detail: {
        nodeId: nodeId,
        agentColor: {
          router: "#00BB81",
          intent: "#FFD500",
          execution: "#64B5F6",
          verify: "#FF6E6E",
          doctor: "#B39DDB"
        }[data.agent_key] || "#00BB81"
      }
    }));
  }
}

Also — when a node pill is rendered in a chat message (the existing createNodePill function), make clicking it do TWO things:
a) Keep the existing behavior (select node on canvas)
b) NEW: Also briefly flash the node. Dispatch the same superduper:node_touch event with agentColor "#00BB81" so the node gets a jade accent bar for a few seconds. This creates a visual "ping" linking chat to canvas.

FILE 2: ui/web/js/node_fx.js

Find the "executing" event listener. When a node starts executing, dispatch an event that the sidebar can listen for:

document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("superduper:node_executing", {
  detail: { nodeId: detail, nodeName: node ? node.title || node.type : "Unknown" }
}));

Find the "executed" event listener. Similarly dispatch:

document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("superduper:node_executed", {
  detail: { nodeId: detail }
}));

Also add: when a node starts executing, auto-pan the canvas to center on that node if it's off-screen. Use this pattern:

const node = app.graph.getNodeById(nodeId);
if (node) {
  const canvas = app.canvas;
  const [nx, ny] = [node.pos[0] + node.size[0]/2, node.pos[1] + node.size[1]/2];
  const visible = canvas.visible_area;
  // Only pan if node is outside visible area
  if (nx < visible[0] || nx > visible[0]+visible[2] || ny < visible[1] || ny > visible[1]+visible[3]) {
    canvas.centerOnNode(node);
  }
}

FILE 3: ui/web/js/sidebar.js (continued)

Listen for the node_executing/node_executed events from node_fx. When a node starts executing, add a small status line to the chat area:

document.addEventListener("superduper:node_executing", (e) => {
  // Only show if we have an active progress panel
  if (!progressPanel) return;
  // Update progress panel with current node name
  updateProgress(progressPanel, { currentNode: e.detail.nodeName });
});

This closes the loop: chat actions highlight nodes, node execution updates the chat. The two panels stay in sync.

